    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d21">

                <pb facs="0094" n="52" sameAs="frus:frus1951v04p1/pg52"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">No. 21</seg>
                </opener>
                <note rend="inline" type="source">
                    ECA message files, FRC 53A278, Paris: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Assistant Administrator for Programs, ECA (</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Porter</hi><hi rendition="#italic">) to
                        the Acting Administrator for Economic Cooperation (</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Wood</hi><hi rendition="#italic">)</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret   priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-08-27T17:00:00+01:00">August 27, 1951—5
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    Repto 4229. Ref Torep 6240.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d21-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>1. Believe manifesto is better than is indicated in your appraisal and that it
                    justifies response proposed in our suggested statement by the President.</p>
                <p>2. We, of course, wld like to see more inspiring document which wld affirm more
                    strongly need for and progress toward Eur unity and wld present more sharply
                    defined action program. We have pushed toward this end in our talks with
                    delegations. Stikker will have dinner with me Tuesday and I
                    shall use occasion to state again US views. I also expect to talk to Gaitskell before Council meeting. I believe it
                    is unrealistic, however, to expect any substantial modification of manifesto
                    along lines you indicate since I believe this is about as far as British are
                    willing to go at this time.</p>
                <p>3. Blaisdell and Lindeman went to London last week and accompanied by Batt had talks at highest official levels in
                    Cabinet, office, Treasury and Defense Dept and made some progress in obtaining
                    more positive and cooperative approach by Brit.</p>
                <p>It is unfortunate that preparation of statement has coincided with absence of
                    many ministers on holiday. However, I doubt that even if ministers had been
                    readily available, fundamental policy decision looking toward European unity wld
                    have been made in time to be reflected in this document.</p>
                <p>4. I believe approach to coal problem proposed in Repto 4077<anchor n="2" xml:id="d21-f2"/> is more meaningful than
                    attempt to define in this document specific steps to raise coal production.
                    There is much hard work yet to be done before Brit and Gers especially can be
                    induced to take these steps.</p>
                <pb facs="0095" n="53" xml:id="pg53"/>
                <p>5. I wld greatly appreciate knowing Tuesday before I see Dr.
                        Stikker what indication can give him concerning the
                    American response.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d21-f3"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Porter</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d21-f1" n="1" xml:id="d21-f1-content">
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Supra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d21-f2" n="2" xml:id="d21-f2-content">
                <p>Document 71.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d21-f3" n="3" xml:id="d21-f3-content">
                <p>In priority telegram Torep 6279 to Paris,
                    August 27, Foster informed Porter that “After discussion here believe
                    separate statements Manifesto should be issued by Acheson and Foster
                    morning August 30. Will cable tomorrow text Foster statement based on modification your draft.” (ECA message files, FRC 53A278, Paris)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
